  ('jpmorgan-kinexys-formerly-jpm-coin', 'JPMorgan Kinexys (formerly JPM Coin)', 'monetary-access-rails', 'institutional-payment-rails', 'https://www.jpmorgan.com/kinexys', ARRAY['Ethereum Mainnet (select pilots and interoperability layers)', 'private permissioned networks']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "JPMorgan Kinexys is JPMorgan’s blockchain-based institutional payment network that enables real-time, tokenized deposit settlement and treasury flows for global enterprises, with selective integration and interoperability with Ethereum-based assets and standards.", "extras": {"Abstraction Risk": "Fully Ethereum-Abstracted", "Availability / SLA Expectations": "Bank-grade / enterprise SLAs (24/7 intraday settlement)", "Custody Model": "Bank-managed custody and account structures", "Ethereum Role in Stack": "Anchored / finality layer (Ethereum-inspired and selectively integrated; public Ethereum used for interoperability and asset tokenization initiatives)", "Failure Mode": "Settlement confined to bank network; public-chain connectivity paused", "Geographic Scope": "Global (bank client footprint)", "Headquarters / Primary Jurisdiction": "United States", "Institutional Adoption Level": "High (live production usage with major corporates)", "Interaction with DeFi": "None (permissioned, non-DeFi)", "Interaction with On-Ramps": "None (direct institutional banking access)", "Interaction with Stablecoins": "Optional / complementary (prefers tokenized deposits over third-party stablecoins)", "Is Ethereum Abstracted from End Users?": "Yes (fully abstracted; bank-native interfaces)", "KYC / AML Enforcement Level": "Institutional-grade (bank-level compliance)", "Maintaining Organization": "JPMorgan Chase & Co.", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Does this entity use Ethereum as a backend or anchored settlement layer for institutional-grade payment flows, even if users never touch Ethereum directly? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "Kinexys represents the bank-led abstra