  ('hyperledger-besu-enterprise-ethereum-settlement-stacks', 'Hyperledger Besu (Enterprise Ethereum Settlement Stacks)', 'monetary-access-rails', 'institutional-payment-rails', 'https://besu.hyperledger.org', ARRAY['Ethereum Mainnet', 'private Ethereum networks', 'Ethereum L2 and rollup-compatible environments']::text[], ARRAY[]::text[], '{"description": "Hyperledger Besu is an enterprise-grade, open-source Ethereum client used by institutions to run permissioned or public Ethereum networks for payment settlement, tokenized cash, and programmable financial workflows.", "extras": {"Abstraction Risk": "Ethereum-Abstracted", "Availability / SLA Expectations": "Enterprise-grade (operator-defined SLAs)", "Custody Model": "Client-managed custody; integrations with enterprise wallets and qualified custodians", "Ethereum Role in Stack": "Native settlement layer (full Ethereum execution and consensus client)", "Failure Mode": "Network misconfiguration; client-operated node outages", "Geographic Scope": "Global", "Headquarters / Primary Jurisdiction": "Global / Open-source foundation", "Institutional Adoption Level": "Medium–High (widely adopted in enterprise pilots and production systems)", "Interaction with DeFi": "Limited / controlled (permissioned or policy-restricted usage)", "Interaction with On-Ramps": "None (settlement infrastructure only)", "Interaction with Stablecoins": "Primary settlement medium (issuer-agnostic, protocol-native)", "Is Ethereum Abstracted from End Users?": "Yes (end users interact through enterprise applications and workflows)", "KYC / AML Enforcement Level": "Institutional-grade (implemented at application and workflow layer)", "Maintaining Organization": "Hyperledger Foundation (Linux Foundation), with primary contributions from ConsenSys", "Practitioner Validation Check": "Does this entity provide Ethereum-based settlement infrastructure for institutional-grade payment flows, even if end users never interact with Ethereum directly? Yes", "Pract