oes Ethereum materially enable settlement within that region? Yes", "Practitioner’s Note": "Bitso is the canonical LatAm Ethereum payments rail: success depends less on DeFi composability and more on banking relationships, corridor liquidity, and regulatory durability across volatile FX environments.", "Primary Dependency Risks": "Local banking partners, regulatory changes, stablecoin liquidity", "Primary Function": "Regional cross-border payments and settlement", "Primary Jurisdiction(s)": "Mexico; regional licenses/registrations across LatAm", "Primary Region / Geography Served": "Latin America (Mexico core; Brazil, Argentina, Colombia)", "Primary Settlement Currency": "USD stablecoins", "Reason for Inclusion": "Bitso qualifies as a Regional Payment Network because its core product is geographically constrained to Latin America and uses Ethereum-based stablecoin settlement to solve FX inefficiency, remittance friction, and local banking access issues.", "Regional Adoption Level": "High", "Regional Constraint Type": "FX / Banking access", "Regulatory Posture": "Locally licensed / regulated crypto and payments provider", "Settlement Asset Types": "Stablecoins (USDC primarily; USDT secondary)", "Settlement vs Access Orientation": "Settlement-First", "Systemic Importance to Ethereum (Regional)": "High", "Target User Segment": "Remittance providers, enterprises, fintechs, SMBs", "Transaction Scale": "Mixed (high-volume remittances; high-value B2B flows)"}, "source_label": "Regional Payment Networks"}'::jsonb)
) AS v(slug, name, sector_slug, subsector_slug, website, chains, tags, meta)
JOIN public.sectors sec ON sec.slug = v.sector_slug
JOIN public.subsectors s ON s.sector_id = sec.id AND s.slug = v.subsector_slug
ON CONFLICT (slug) DO UPDATE SET
  name = EXCLUDED.name,
  subsector_id = EXCLUDED.subsector_id,
  website = EXCLUDED.website,
  chains = EXCLUDED.chains,
  tags = EXCLUDED.tags,
  meta = EXCLUDED.meta,
  updated_at = NOW();
